We've seen previews of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> running on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>, including a new StandBy mode that activates even when the iPhone isn't charging. Apple showed the mode in press materials, but leaker pdfu <a href="https://x.com/itspdfu/status/2104567049963921785">today shared</a> a more in-depth look at some of the options.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-weather.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063440" /><br/>
There are multiple StandBy faces available on the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;, five of which we weren't aware of.<br/>
<br/>
A Home Camera view will show a single camera feed or a grid of up to nine camera feeds. There's a Home Modular option that likely shows smart home controls, and a Snoopy-themed face.<br/>
<br/>
